cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite it as below. If you use its results or data,
  please also cite the two datasets listed under references.
title: "Musico: a two-stage music recommender on Music4All-Onion"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Zunhong
    family-names: Mei
repository-code: "https://github.com/JWYQuentin/Musico--The-Music-Recommendation-System"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A two-tower retrieval model (PyTorch) followed by a gradient-boosted LambdaRank
  ranker (XGBoost), trained on 17.5 million Last.fm listens from Music4All-Onion,
  scored on a split by time against popularity, item-kNN and ALS, with a
  popularity-bias and genre-fairness analysis and a local recommendation API.
keywords:
  - recommender systems
  - music recommendation
  - two-tower retrieval
  - learning to rank
  - popularity bias
